    'content' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Chennai is one of India's busiest gateways for imported goods. Cargo comes in through Chennai Port, Kamarajar Port at Ennore, Kattupalli and the Chennai air cargo terminal, and Tamil Nadu is home to thousands of packers of food, cosmetics, electronics and consumer goods. If any of those goods are <strong>pre-packaged for sale</strong>, the business behind them needs an <strong>LMPC certificate</strong>.</p>
<p>From our team in Bangalore, Karnataka, Instacertify has been making LMPC certification simple for importers and packers in Chennai and across Tamil Nadu, so they stay compliant while importing and selling packaged commodities. This guide explains when you need LMPC, which route to choose and how we get it done.</p>

<h2>What Is an LMPC Certificate?</h2>
<p>LMPC stands for <strong>Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities)</strong>. Under Rule 27 of the Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011, every manufacturer, packer and importer of pre-packaged commodities must register with the Legal Metrology authorities. The registration certificate is what businesses call the LMPC certificate.</p>
<p>It confirms that your firm is registered and follows the rules for packaged goods: correct net quantity, a proper MRP and the declarations buyers rely on. For the rules in detail, see our <a href="/resources/blogs/lmpc-certificate-registration-rules-eligibility-fee-rule27">complete guide to LMPC registration and Rule 27</a>.</p>

<h2>Why Customs Asks for LMPC When You Import</h2>
<p>When you import a packaged commodity from outside India, <strong>customs checks that your firm complies with the Legal Metrology rules for packaged goods</strong>. To confirm this, customs officers may ask for your LMPC certificate along with the labels on the goods.</p>
<p>Without it, a shipment can be held at the port until the paperwork is in order, and relabelling goods after arrival adds cost and delay. Getting your LMPC certificate before the first consignment lands keeps clearance at Chennai smooth. Importers should also read our <a href="/resources/blogs/lmpc-compliance-requirements-importer-2026">LMPC requirements for importers</a>.</p>

<h2>Packers Need LMPC Too</h2>
<p>LMPC is not only for importers. If you <strong>pack or repack products for sale</strong>, the Packaged Commodities Rules make packer registration mandatory, even if the product itself is made by someone else. Common examples from Chennai and Tamil Nadu businesses:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Packaged sweets and snacks</strong> sold in boxes and pouches</li>
<li><strong>Sunglasses and eyewear</strong> packed in branded cases</li>
